  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a substantive denial that requires an appeal to overturn. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is the most effective next step to challenge the medical necessity and separate the service from the bundled one. The previous P2P request likely did not result in a reversal, so a formal appeal with medical necessity documentation is the appropriate escalation path to progress the claim.",
